 "content_notes": "Tone: remarkable and ironic, never mocking. Cassie Sainsbury (convicted after a guilty plea, Bogota, November 2017; paroled April 2020) appears only as a faceless silhouette tagged NOT A LIKENESS; her account that her family was threatened is reported as her claim. The officers, the judge, the gym client and the young man in the lesson are generic figures, never named; no badge, crest or insignia of any real force or court. Headphones and their boxes are generic (no brand, no logo); the 'drugs' are plain white bundles, no drug use is shown, no weapon, no violence. The DEA tip-off is attributed to Colombian police. The statistic card names its source. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue is invented. Status verified 2026-10-16.",
